# Summary of changes for run 8ca6e961-3a5c-468c-98a3-0d537ccec609
Five sorry-free Lean files in Catalog/Physics/ formalise the METHOD-LOCALITY verdict, all building against Mathlib with only standard axioms, plus three reports. MethodLocalityFactorLocal.lean gives a collision-time calculus, shows Pollard rho's update commutes with reduction from ZMod N to ZMod p and hence is exactly cofactor flat (ratio 1, against the measured x1.40) with pigeonhole bound p, proves a reveal lemma turning a mod-p collision into a nontrivial proper divisor, the honest probabilistic form of the sqrt(p) birthday law, the exact trial-division ledger minFac N - 1 (slope exactly 1 in p, matching the measured 1.09) together with a counterexample to its cofactor flatness (cost 2 at 4093*3 versus 4092 at 4093*4093), and the kernel-verified anchor that the rho orbit of x to x^2+1 from seed 2 modulo 4093 first repeats at step exactly 70, at least 58 times cheaper than trial division; a critique theorem shows the 0.45 exponent is not a worst case, since the successor map on ZMod p costs exactly p. MethodLocalityPolynomialECM.lean and MethodLocalityNaturality.lean identify the mechanism as naturality: every integer-polynomial iteration, and more generally every uniform step commuting with all ring maps, is cofactor flat and bounded by p, with rho, its cubic variant and the p-1 exponentiation step as instances, while ECM's stage-1 ledger is computed exactly inside the CRT product group where the cofactor order cancels identically, the expected curve count being bounded by the Hasse ceiling of the factor and equal to 1 at the wall. MethodLocalityRigidity.lean proves that a cost model reading only the modulus and cofactor flat must be constant on composites, so trial division's non-flatness is forced rather than accidental, while rho's ledger provably reads the factor (1 step at p = 3, 70 at p = 4093), and a second kernel-verified anchor (p = 1009, rho time 49) gives the widening advantage 20x to 58x. MethodLocalityCRT.lean decomposes the collision of a run modulo